CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785714477
OL,3,CMore than one in 10 householders do
OL,4,Cnot intend to abide by hosepipe ban
OL,6,FOther reasons given for ignoring a ban
OL,7,Fwere concerns about fruit and
OL,8,Fvegetables going to waste because they
OL,9,Fwere too difficult to water with a
OL,10,Fwatering can, and to support wildlife
OL,11,Fin the garden.
OL,13,FHouseholds subject to a ban can use a
OL,14,Fwatering can, and using a hosepipe is
OL,15,Fstill allowed to water food crops at
OL,16,Fhome or on an allotment when using a
OL,17,Fwatering can is not practical.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
