OL,3,CMore than one in 10 householders do
OL,4,Cnot intend to abide by hosepipe ban
OL,6,FConsumer Council for Water chief
OL,7,Fexecutive Mike Keil said: "We know
OL,8,Fhosepipe restrictions are frustrating
OL,9,Ffor some people, but water companies
OL,10,Fhave a duty to act when sustained hot,
OL,11,Fdry weather and increased demand for
OL,12,Fwater threaten both the environment
OL,13,Fand the security of water supplies
OL,14,Fneeded for essential use.
OL,26,@oD@[OU
